  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `CampaignParameter` struct documentation in `CampaignParameters.sol` explicitly states strict requirements for the duration parameter:\n\n```solidity\n/// @notice Total duration of the campaign in seconds\n    /// @dev Must be a multiple of EPOCH_DURATION (3600 seconds / 1 hour)\n    /// @dev Must be at least EPOCH_DURATION (1 hour minimum)\n    uint32 duration;\n```\n\n\nHowever, the `DistributionCreator.sol` contract (specifically `_createCampaign` and `overrideCampaign`) only enforces the minimum duration, but fails to enforce the \"multiple of EPOCH_DURATION\" requirement.\n\n```solidity\n\n// DistributionCreator.sol :: _createCampaign\nfunction _createCampaign(CampaignParameters memory newCampaign) internal returns (bytes32) {\n    // ...\n    // Check: Duration >= HOUR\n    if (newCampaign.duration < HOUR) revert Errors.CampaignDurationBelowHour();\n    \n    // MISSING: Check that duration % HOUR == 0\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n\nhttps://docs.merkl.xyz/merkl-mechanisms/features?q=computation+schedule#campaigns-of-any-duration\n\n### Impact \n\n- Data Consistency & Reward Calculation Errors: The Merkl protocol relies on discrete 1-hour epochs (EPOCH_DURATION) for reward calculation and distribution.\n\n - Partial Epochs: If a creator sets a duration of 5400 seconds (1.5 hours), the campaign covers one full epoch and one half-epoch.\n\n- Off-chain Failure: If the off-chain indexing engine strictly expects aligned epochs, it may either reject the campaign entirely (locking user funds) or drop the final partial epoch (causing a loss of user rewards)\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n- Add a modulo check in _createCampaign (and overrideCampaign if necessary) to enforce that the duration is perfectly aligned with the epoch length.\n\n```solidity\nfunction _createCampaign(CampaignParameters memory newCampaign) internal returns (bytes32) {\n        uint256 rewardTokenMinAmount = rewardTokenMinAmounts[newCampaign.rewardToken];\n        \n        if (newCampaign.duration < HOUR) revert Errors.CampaignDurationBelowHour();\n+       if (newCampaign.duration % HOUR != 0) revert Errors.InvalidParam();\n\n        // ... rest of the function\n    }\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "- Run this in the `c4-test` Directory.\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity ^0.8.17;\n\nimport { Fixture } from \"../Fixture.t.sol\";\nimport { CampaignParameters } from \"../../contracts/struct/CampaignParameters.sol\";\nimport { console } from \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n\ncontract C4DurationMultiplePoC is Fixture {\n    uint256 internal constant amount = 100e18;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        // 1. Whitelist token with small min-per-epoch so tests pass easily\n        vm.startPrank(guardian);\n        address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        tokens[0] = address(angle);\n        amounts[0] = 1e8; // Tiny min threshold\n        creator.setRewardTokenMinAmounts(tokens, amounts);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // 2. Fund and approve Alice\n        angle.mint(address(alice), amount * 10);\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        angle.approve(address(creator), type(uint256).max);\n    }\n\n    // PoC : Creation allows a duration that is NOT a multiple of HOUR (e.g., 5400 = 1.5 hours)\n    function test_CreateCampaign_AllowsNonMultipleDuration() external {\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n\n        uint32 badDuration = 5400; // 1.5 hours, violates struct docs\n        uint32 start = uint32(block.timestamp + 1 hours);\n\n        CampaignParameters memory c = CampaignParameters({\n            campaignId: bytes32(0),\n            creator: alice,\n            rewardToken: address(angle),\n            amount: amount,\n            campaignType: 0,\n            startTimestamp: start,\n            duration: badDuration,\n            campaignData: bytes(\"\")\n        });\n\n        // Expect no revert even though docs require duration % HOUR == 0\n        bytes32 campaignId = creator.createCampaign(c);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Verify on-chain state reflects invalid (per docs) duration\n        CampaignParameters memory stored = creator.campaign(campaignId);\n        console.log(\"Created campaign with duration:\", stored.duration);\n        console.log(\"Duration % HOUR:\", stored.duration % EPOCH_DURATION);\n        assertEq(stored.duration, badDuration, \"Stored duration should match the invalid value\");\n        assertTrue(stored.duration % EPOCH_DURATION != 0, \"Duration is not a multiple of HOUR\");\n    }\n\n}\n```",
